# Project Rules for Django + DRF + PostgreSQL Backend and React.js Frontend

## Backend (Django + DRF)
- Use Python 3.11+ and Django 5.x conventions
- Use DRF ViewSets + Routers, NOT function-based views
- Use django-filter for filtering
- Use JWT authentication via djangorestframework-simplejwt
- Every model must have created_at and updated_at timestamp fields
- Every model must have a docstring explaining its purpose
- Every API view must have explicit permission_classes defined
- Never invent Django/DRF settings or packages that don't exist - ask before adding a new dependency
- Keep all backend code in backend/ directory
- Use snake_case for Python code (variables, functions, classes, files)
- Write a short comment above any non-obvious business rule referencing which requirement it satisfies (e.g., # FR-08: unique case identifier)

## Frontend (React.js)
- Keep all frontend code in frontend/ directory
- Use camelCase for JavaScript/React code (variables, functions, components)

## General
- Follow Django and DRF best practices
- Maintain clear separation between backend and frontend codebases
